.resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-cr10.md:3:The CR7/CR8/CR9 verdicts form one family: canonical shape or outer-walk position accepted in place of cross-record authority for the profile pair. Review the census first: it must enumerate every (event kind x relationship) row of SPEC 5.2's pair rule with 2.4/5.4 — provider.launched first/later, task_board.launched first/later, session.resumed, fork.created — each with its authority input (Session Record; effective profile at the REFERENCED checkpoint's own event-head closure resolved through checkpoint_id and the admitted Checkpoint Record), owner arm, positive control, negatives (missing/read-failed/contradictory/non-newest/later-local-only/losing-lease/wrong-session) and narrowing plant. An undriven row that is not a named caller bound with its owning clause is a finding. Then verify the shared owner (checkCheckpointProfileAuthority / checkClosureProfilePairs / checkProfilePairSource) against the census: rerun TestReview9ForkLocalProfile and TestReview9ResumeReferencedCheckpoint on the exact candidate (both negatives must now refuse with the pinned class, controls pass), and probe at least one census row the producer did not witness through BuildPlan, fresh and old-plan Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus and AuthoritativeList across direct/task_board and winner/necessary-ancestor. Confirm the resume expectation is derived from the referenced checkpoint closure, not from the outer walk, and that historical/branching/lagging controls still admit.
.resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-cr9.md:3:Reproduce TestRev8CheckpointProfileAuthority on the exact candidate: the four valid creation-profile/null controls and the missing profile.changed reference negatives across direct/task_board persistence and winner/necessary-ancestor checkpoints, through BuildPlan, fresh and old-plan Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus and AuthoritativeList. Then review the complete assigned C6 consumption semantics against pinned Section 5.4 and the referenced 2.4/5.2 using actual canonical payload, Session Record and closure inputs: valid subsequent profile.changed references; missing, non-newest, losing-lease and other wrong-authority references; historical, branching and lagging controls; old-plan authority substitution. New tests alone do not prove completeness: inspect the shared production owner checkCheckpointProfileAuthority and every callsite. Future materialization APIs are not delegation; canonical shape, digest or lease tuple are not profile-source semantics. Preserve the accepted CLI/publication/storage/transport/effects boundary without narrowing the consumer contract.
.resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev7.md:2:The failed class audit is C6: checkpoint event authority was delegated to APIs that lack event repositories/closure inputs. Implement actual shared admission of required checkpoint event-head closure against Session/Lease relationships for winner AND every necessary ancestor, used by BuildPlan, old-plan Revalidate and both summaries. Preserve valid historical heads, not equality with current tails; preserve branching/lagging. Missing references, unavailable source reads, cross-session or later/losing-lease facts must be distinguished per pinned contracts. Use existing production repository/attestation/reducer boundaries as appropriate; no synthetic digest placeholders or caller-trusted validation claims.
