.resources/TASK-260922-31qyyi/TASK-260922-31qyyi_producer.md:3:WHY THIS EXISTS — A HALF-CLOSED SECURITY PROPERTY. Pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §2.4 (Execution profiles, line 646; the clause at line 666): losing-lease or ambiguous events MUST NOT change the effective profile. BUG-260917-3lddu0 (landed in PR #57, trunk `40bb8c9`) closed this only **through append admission**: `sessrepo.checkWinningLease` now refuses an append under a superseded lease. But `sessprofile.Derive` takes `(record, events)` and cannot see the lease store at all, so a losing event that extends its own lease's tail is a perfectly continuous chain to it. The 3lddu0 reviewer proved it: with the append gate disabled as an instrument in a copy, **probe 15 still yields `{Profile: yolo, HasSource: true}`** at `Projector.Project` — a losing writer drives the session to `yolo` with `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`. Any other path that admits such an event (a future writer, a replay, a restore) reopens the hole. This leaf gives the property an owner **independent of the append gate**. Read BUG-260917-3lddu0's verdicts rev1-rev3 and its results before writing anything; the probe bodies are in `TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz` (probes 9 and 15).
.resources/TASK-260922-31qyyi/TASK-260922-31qyyi_review-verdict-rev1.md:12:In the committed tree, all 8 derivation witnesses call `t.Skip`: 4 losing-lease and 4 ambiguous (ev/pkg-tests.log). My narrowing M1 (`authorizedSource` returns true for any known lease, which admits every losing-lease tail) produced **zero failures in the committed suite**. Only the instrumented copy killed it (ev/mutants.log). M2 (knownLease matches on epoch only) behaves the same way. So CI would accept a regression that brings probe 15 back.
