.resources/TASK-260922-31qyyi/TASK-260922-31qyyi_rework-rev2.md:5:1. **P1 — the property has no live witness in CI, because all eight of your derivation tests skip.** Four losing-lease and four ambiguous tests call `t.Skip` in the committed tree. The reviewer's narrowing M1 — `authorizedSource` returns true for any known lease, admitting every losing-lease tail — produced **zero failures** in the committed suite, and so did M2 (`knownLease` matching on epoch only). Only the instrumented copy killed them. So CI would accept a regression that brings probe 15 back. This is exactly the trap your brief warned about, arriving from the other side: last time a test asserted the upstream gate's refusal and never reached the property; this time the tests step aside because the gate would block their setup. Neither is a witness.
