 [`internal/merkleinventory`](internal/merkleinventory) is a separate in-memory
-Mesh RPC 2 component for deterministic namespace roots/children, schema
-membership, and bounded JSON object retrieval. It is not wired into the
-authenticated Host Channel handler, does not persist inventories or transfer
-chunks, and does not advertise an anti-entropy capability. RPC 3/4/5 inventory
-membership and their added authority rules remain unsupported by this
-component. Its validation boundaries and test commands are documented in the
+Mesh RPC 2 component for deterministic namespace roots/children, validated
+membership, and bounded JSON object retrieval. It carries separate proofs for
+the exact synthetic-ID inventory fixture and a real-byte in-process union;
+the identity-only proof does not claim object validation. Four mapped schemas
+remain fail-closed pending their owning validators. The package is not wired
+into the authenticated Host Channel handler, does not persist inventories or
+transfer chunks, and advertises no anti-entropy capability. RPC 3/4 inventory
+serving is outside this component's scope (SPEC §§11.8–11.9); RPC 5 authority
+rules also remain unsupported. Validation boundaries and commands are in the
 package README, [conformance matrix](internal/merkleinventory/CONFORMANCE-MATRIX.md),
