 - IMPLEMENTATION: `internal/merkleinventory` adds deterministic Section 11.4 roots/children, schema-owned membership, bounded `inventory.roots` / `inventory.children` / `objects.get`, and in-process differing-node retrieval. Section 10.7 Tombstone and Acknowledgement identity validation now admits their complete closed shapes; acknowledgement admission requires its stored Tombstone and matching subject. No Host Channel handler or capability advertisement was added.
-- CONFORMANCE: the production trie reproduces empty/singleton/branch fixtures, child hashes and all six MIXED-NS-1 roots. N1 pins the valid six-root fixture, models Descriptor-as-record / independent Chunk / local-marker membership, and demonstrates root divergence only in `record`, `manifest`, and `blob`. The exact combined MIXED-NS-EXCHANGE byte fixture remains unclaimed because its synthetic Checkpoint/Descriptor IDs have no supplied bytes; four mapped schema rows also remain fail-closed, and lease-head/divergent-event rules remain with the Story union owner. Producer property coverage is 2 of 4 fully driven.
