+- CONFORMANCE: the production trie reproduces empty/singleton/branch fixtures, child hashes and all six MIXED-NS-1 roots. N1 pins the valid six-root fixture, models Descriptor-as-record / independent Chunk / local-marker membership, and demonstrates root divergence only in `record`, `manifest`, and `blob`. After orchestrator decision rev1, MIXED-NS-EXCHANGE has two separate proofs: exact synthetic IDs through identity-level serving/walking/convergence with no object-validation claim, and validated exchange through real bytes with roots pinned to those bytes. Four mapped schema rows remain fail-closed as directed, each with a literal refusal test, unchanged roots/counts, no quarantine, and a row-specific admitting narrowing. Lease-head/divergent-event rules remain with the Story union owner. Producer property coverage is 4 of 4 rows driven, with four explicit validator bounds.
